{"time_unix": 1793967076.9628162, "event": "candidate_created", "payload": {"id": "exp5-percpu-slot-batch-v1", "parent": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_candidate": null, "generation": 1, "baseline_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "brief_id": "brief-000001-f3113be57b02", "worktree": "worktrees/exp5-percpu-slot-batch-2026-11-06/exp5-percpu-slot-batch-v1", "status": "active", "hypothesis": "In mm/swapfile.c, cluster_alloc_swap_entry() and swap_alloc_fast() acquire spinlocks (ci->lock and si->lock) for every single page allocation. Reserving a batch of contiguous swap slots (e.g. 16 to 64 entries) per-CPU in percpu_swap_cluster amortizes lock acquisition, atomic accounting, and cluster scanning over the batch while safely releasing any unallocated slots on flush/swapoff, reducing swapout latency without wasting unallocated slots. Reject if candidate leaks swap slots, corrupts swap cache, fails correctness gates, or fails calibrated screening.", "created_unix": 1793967076.9621005, "protocol_sha256": "8ef325db29ae99b28c1d636162c693ed47d136d865ad2494eee61c58d8ceb9ad", "mechanism": {"kind": "reviewed_structure", "claim": "In mm/swapfile.c, percpu_swap_cluster maintains an order-0 batched swap slot reservation, refilling up to 32 contiguous entries under ci->lock with a single swap_range_alloc() update and serving subsequent order-0 allocations directly without redundant spinlock contention or list manipulations, releasing unused slots on device flush.", "falsifier": "Exact-tree review shows lost lifetime protection, incorrect slot conflict handling, or broken cache lookup fallback. Correctness, metadata spread <1%, and calibrated fast-tier screen independently gate execution."}}}
